	"naming": {
		"_about": "Names from long-time holders (Items.naming, decision 365). A thing with a verb, or tagged armour or tool, carried by one named holder (a player, a companion) held_days of the world clock (DayNight.day_steps; while they are in the world) with deeds or more done with it, takes a name for life from lore's forms, and one strength: the one whose from is the deed its namer did most with it. Each strength changes how its verb works, never its damage: guard_stamina (times what guarding costs), draw (times a bow's draw times), brace_ticks (the steps still before a spear is braced), noise (times the fight noise of its blows), down_ticks (added to a knockdown), dread (World.holder_dread: enemy-ai reads it). A deed with no strength (struck) gives none.",
		"held_days": 2.0,
		"deeds": 10,
		"strengths": {
			"steady": {"from": "guarded", "guard_stamina": 0.75},
			"quick": {"from": "shot", "draw": 0.8},
			"set": {"from": "braced", "brace_ticks": 3},
			"quiet": {"from": "behind", "noise": 0.5},
			"heavy": {"from": "downed", "down_ticks": 5},
			"dread": {"from": "felled", "dread": true}
		}
	},
	"curse": {
		"_about": "Cursed heirlooms (Items.curse, decision 370). A named thing taken by anyone but its namer, other than from the namer's own hand (off the ground, out of a chest or the stockpile, from a monster's spill), is kept from its namer until it is back in the namer's hands. While kept, a holder it counts for gathers ill, 0 to 1 over full_days of the world clock held, and loses it at fade of that rate while not holding it. follows: thing (every holder but the namer) or taker (only who took it); Jeff's question, thing until he answers. below_baseline: whether ill may take the holder below baseline (true: noticed farther off, slower mending) or only shortens their buffs (false); null until Jeff answers, and until then ill does nothing.",
		"follows": "thing",
		"below_baseline": null,
		"full_days": 1.0,
		"fade": 0.5
	}
}
